M88M is a modern, cross-platform port of the classic PC-8801 emulator
M88, originally developed by cisc.  While the original M88 was
tightly coupled with the Win32 API and DirectX, M88M leverages
raylib and raygui for its frontend, making it natively compatible
with macOS (Intel/Apple Silicon), Linux, FreeBSD, Haiku, and Windows
via a single CMake-based build system.
